%description:

Tcp.lossUndoEnabled:off -- the reduction of a spurious fast retransmission stays.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Undo a spurious cwnd/ssthresh reduction when D-SACK (RFC 2883) or
timestamps (RFC 3522 Eifel) reveal the retransmission was unnecessary".

The classes: off (false, the default) and on (true, the value of LinuxTcp), with the facets
dsack and eifel. The code: Rfc6675Recovery::step4() and onRexmitTimeout() keep the window and
the threshold of before the reduction (undoInit()); Rfc6675Recovery::segmentsAcked() restores
them when each retransmission of the episode has a D-SACK (noteDsack()), or when an ACK echoes
a timestamp older than the first retransmission (packetDelayed(), RFC 3522). The undo needs
SACK. This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host1, which sends 200000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms, and the tap delays the 30th data
segment by 5 ms once, so that the next segments pass it and host2 SACKs them. RACK
retransmits the 30th segment at the third SACK, before the late original arrives: a spurious
fast retransmission. Observation: level 2, no value of the signal ssthresh above 1e8 in 1 s after the reduction.

%# parameter: Tcp.lossUndoEnabled
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.lossUndoEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpLossUndoEnabledOff")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 41992 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).delay(0.005)
                     .describe("the 30th data segment of host1, the first time: 5 ms late"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .describe("the reduction at the fast retransmission")
                  .within(2.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                   .filterValueAtLeast(1e8)
                   .describe("an undo of the reduction")
                   .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpLossUndoEnabledOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.lossUndoEnabled = false    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 200000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpLossUndoEnabledOff: PASS
